author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The gate runner records a structured failure document naming the failing gate, its exit status, and its captured verdict, at a path supplied by the environment; The blocked-release issue renders its cause from that document when it exists, including the blocking issue identifiers and the per-issue reason the gate assigned; The preflight configuration detection is retained only as the fallback used when no failure document was produced; No part of the mechanism classifies failures by matching patterns against log or message text; A negative control proves the rendered cause changes when the recorded gate verdict changes, and that a missing document still yields the preflight fallback"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Blocked-release reporting now preserves the structured verdict of the failing gate or downstream workflow stage.
expected_result: "The blocked-release issue names the machine-readable failing stage/status and gate blockers when available, falling back to preflight only when no record exists, without log-text classification."
actual_result: "The auto-release workflow records gate, workflow job/step, discovery, GitHub Release verification, and npm verification failures; rendering and negative controls pass."
